  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...The strong westerly winds will ease late this \nafternoon into the evening.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nSo far as of early Monday afternoon, the highest winds have \nbeen in Northern Maine, with 35 to 50 mph gusts and isolated \npower outages, with not quite as much wind Bangor/Downeast with \ngusts topping out 25 to 35 mph. The highest gusts have occurred\nfor most areas by early this afternoon, and winds will steadily\ndecrease through the rest of the afternoon and drop pretty fast\naround sunset. Any additional damage should be before 5pm.\nWind chills atop Katahdin will remain in the teens through the \nevening.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Frost expected Downeast tonight with low\ntemperatures approaching freezing.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure building in behind the departing low pressure\nsystem should lead to clearing skies this evening, which in \ncombination with decreasing winds should allow for strong \novernight cooling. Temperatures are expected to dip into the low\nto mid 30s tonight over Downeast where the growing season is \nstill active. Areas to widespread frost are likely and thus a \nFrost Advisory is in effect. Opted to expand the frost advisory \nsouth to the coast. While do not think the very immediate coast \nwill get frost, feel that you will only have to go inland a mile\nor two to see some frost, so expanded the advisory to the \ncoastal zones. Some high clouds will be moving in very late in\nthe night, but do not think they will be fast enough to limit\ncooling especially in the area under the frost advisory.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Light rain is likely late Wednesday into Thursday.\nLittle to no drought relief expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3 DESCRIPTION...\nThickening clouds through the day Wednesday with perhaps some\nsprinkles mainly over the north by midday. Rain chances\ngradually increase late Wednesday and into Wednesday night, and\npersist into Thursday. This is associated with an approaching \ncold front that will move through during the day Thursday. All \ntogether, rainfall from this system looks pretty light late \nWednesday into Thursday, with totals generally one tenth to one \nthird inch in the north and zero to one tenth of an inch \nDowneast.",
